     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5100 mg/day**. That's twice the labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin (2550 mg/day) and well above the extended-release maximum (2000 mg/day). Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and serious stomach and bowel side effects, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Common doses that may be what you meant:**\n- **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals.** This is 2550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum.\n- **850 mg by mouth twice daily.** This is 1700 mg/day total.\n- **1000 mg by mouth twice daily.** This is 2000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do mean 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm and give a short reason, and I'll include that reason in the order note."
      }
     ],
